:"229 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Benson, E"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"This course is NOT intended for Graphic Design majors. Some seats are reserved for A&D majors, A&D minors, and non-A&D majors. If you receive a \"reserve closed\" error, all seats for your major are filled, check back on December 1. Any available seats left on December 1 will be made available to all majors."},{"crn":"58747","code":"2","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["T","R"],"start":1020,"end":1180,"location":"229 Art and Design Building","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"This course is NOT intended for Graphic Design majors. Some seats are reserved for A&D majors, A&D minors, and non-A&D majors. If you receive a \"reserve closed\" error, all seats for your major are filled, check back on December 1. Any available seats left on December 1 will be made available to all majors"}]},{"id":"ARTD 218","title":"Interaction Design Foundation","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"65186","code":"GD1","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":1000,"location":"216 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Blazek, K"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""},{"crn":"65187","code":"GD2","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["T","R"],"start":570,"end":730,"location":"208 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Blazek, K"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""},{"crn":"72157","code":"GD3","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["M","W"],"start":540,"end":700,"location":"208 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Kim, P"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"ARTD 228","title":"Computer Applications","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"63648","code":"1","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":1000,"location":"224 Art and Design Building","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""},{"crn":"51410","code":"2","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["T","R"],"start":1020,"end":1180,"location":"224 Art and Design Building","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"ARTD 299","title":"Spec Topics in Design Courses","creditHours":"1 TO 5 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"48590","code":"CHP","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["M","W"],"start":600,"end":680,"location":"316 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Robinson, S"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Chancellor's Scholar-CHPHonors students."],"note":"In this introductory multimedia studio course, students will speculate about equitable futures by reading and viewing current trends, cultures, movements and key figures to create artistic responses from culturally respective vantage points. The course will touch upon the myriad practices of graphic design. Students will produce and analyze form and content cultural and design understanding."},{"crn":"60164","code":"JDL","type":"Laboratory","partOfTerm":"B","meetings":[{"type":"Laboratory","days":["M","W"],"start":780,"end":940,"location":"340 Art and Design Building","instructors":["De La Rosa, J"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graphic Design or Crafts or History of Art or Photography or Industrial Design or Painting or Sculpture or Art Education or New Media or Industrial Design major(s)."],"note":"Interfaces are never neutral. Every menu, health bar, prompt, and button in a game carries politics. They shape not only how players act but what they are invited to think and feel while acting. This course examines game interfaces and user experience through the lens of critical design, treating UI/UX not as a layer of polish applied after the \"real\" design is done, but as a site where values, arguments, and power relations are built. Drawing on Clark Abt's early framing of serious games as play with purposes beyond entertainment, Ian Bogost's concept of procedural rhetoric (the idea that games persuade through the rules and processes they ask players to enact), and Mary Flanagan's critical play, which treats games as tools for questioning social and cultural norms, we will ask how interface design can reveal, reinforce, or challenge the assumptions embedded in a system. We will pair this with the speculative and critical design tradition of Anthony Dunne and Fiona Raby, who argue that design can provoke reflection rather than simply solve problems, and with game-specific interface scholarship, from Kristine Jørgensen's work on game-world interfaces to Zagal, Björk, and Lewis's analysis of dark patterns that exploit players against their own interests. Throughout the semester, students will analyze existing games, critique conventional usability ideals of \"frictionlessness\" and \"intuitiveness,\" and design their own interface prototypes that use friction, ambiguity, and discomfort deliberately, as means of making players notice, question, and reflect."}]},{"id":"ARTD 317","title":"UI/UX Design for Non-Majors","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"70432","code":"1","type":"Studio","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Studio","days":["M","W"],"start":960,"end":1120,"location":"224 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Kim, P"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Students do NOT need to follow pre-requisites as listed above. ARTD 215 and 217 are not necessary to succeed in this class. Some seats are reserved for A&D majors, A&D minors, and non-A&D majors. If you receive a \"reserve closed\" error, all seats for your major are filled, check back on December 1. Any available seats left on December 1 will be made available to all majors."}]},{"id":"ARTD 326","title":"Sustainability & Manufacturing","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"51827","code":"1","type":"Lecture","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":1000,"location":"331 Art and Design Building","instructors